<title>BELGIUM: GIB negotiating unit sale to KBB.</title>
<headline>GIB negotiating unit sale to KBB.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian retail group GIB confirmed on Tuesday a newspaper report it was in talks to sell its  Sarma department store group to Dutch department store chain  Hema, a unit of NV Koninklijke Bijenkorf Beheer (KBB).</p>
<p>&quot;The impact on the (GIB's) consolidated accounts will be around 200 million Belgian francs, essentially due to the exceptional amortization of assets,&quot; GIB said in a statement.  </p>
<p>GIB said it was selling Sarma because its family clothing business &quot;no longer responds to the needs of a textile sector which is becoming more and more global.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
